IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `oas-core`
IMPORT `oas-core-measures`
IMPORT `oa1-helpers`

-- Old Age Security Act, Part IV, "Adjustment in Consumer Price Index" (s 27) and "Reconsiderations and Appeals" (ss 27.1 and 28): the request
-- for reconsideration by the Minister, the appeal to the Social Security Tribunal, the reference of an income question to the Tax Court of
-- Canada, and the stay of benefits pending judicial review.
-- The ninety days and the longer period the Minister may allow are the Act's (s 27.1(1)); the circumstances in which the Minister may allow a longer
-- period are Regulations s 29.1, piece oa3, and arrive here as an input.
-- Hohfeld: the person's power to request a reconsideration is the Minister's liability; the Minister's duty to reconsider and notify is the person's claim;
-- the person's power to appeal is the Tribunal's liability; the Minister's power to stay payment is the person's liability.

§ `Adjustment in Consumer Price Index`

-- s 27: "a corresponding adjustment shall be made in the Consumer Price Index with respect to any adjustment quarter that is used for the purpose
-- of calculating the amount of any benefit". The Act says nothing about how the adjustment is made, so the adjusted figure is an input
-- elsewhere (fork OA1-F9 of NOTES.md); this rule says only when one must be made.
-- src:835 | 27 Where at any time the Consumer Price Index for Canada, as published by Statistics Canada under the authority of the Statistics Act, is adjusted to reflect a new time basis or a new content basis, a corresponding adjustment shall be made in the Consumer Price Index with respect to any adjustment quarter that is used for the purpose of calculating the amount of any benefit that may be paid under this Act.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 27 (src:835)
GIVEN `the Consumer Price Index for Canada, as published by Statistics Canada under the authority of the Statistics Act, is adjusted to reflect a new time basis or a new content basis` IS A BOOLEAN
      -- out of range: section 2 (piece oas-g0): "Consumer Price Index"; section 9 (piece oa3): Regulations, the average
      `the adjustment quarter is used for the purpose of calculating the amount of a benefit that may be paid under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 27: a corresponding adjustment shall be made in the Consumer Price Index with respect to the adjustment quarter` `the Consumer Price Index for Canada, as published by Statistics Canada under the authority of the Statistics Act, is adjusted to reflect a new time basis or a new content basis` `the adjustment quarter is used for the purpose of calculating the amount of a benefit that may be paid under this Act` MEANS
        `the Consumer Price Index for Canada, as published by Statistics Canada under the authority of the Statistics Act, is adjusted to reflect a new time basis or a new content basis`
    AND `the adjustment quarter is used for the purpose of calculating the amount of a benefit that may be paid under this Act`

§ `Request for reconsideration by Minister`

-- s 27.1(1): "within ninety days after the day on which the person is notified in writing of the decision or determination, or within any longer
-- period that the Minister may, either before or after the expiration of those ninety days, allow". The last day of the longer period, if the
-- Minister has allowed one, is an input.
-- "within ninety days after": the day that is ninety days after is the last day (fork OA1-F15 of NOTES.md).
-- src:839 | 27.1 (1) A person who is dissatisfied with a decision or determination made under this Act that no benefit may be paid to the person, or respecting the amount of a benefit that may be paid to the person, may, within ninety days after the day on which the person is notified in writing of the decision or determination, or within any longer period that the Minister may, either before or after the expiration of those ninety days, allow, make a request to the Minister in the prescribed form and manner for a reconsideration of that decision or determination.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 27.1(1) (src:839)
GIVEN `the day on which the person is notified in writing of the decision or determination` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the person makes the request` IS A DATE
      -- out of range: section 29.1 (piece oa3): Regulations, when the Minister may allow a longer period
      `the last day of the longer period the Minister allows` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 27.1: the request is made within the time allowed` `the day on which the person is notified in writing of the decision or determination` `the day on which the person makes the request` `the last day of the longer period the Minister allows` MEANS
        `the day on which the person makes the request` AT MOST (`the day that is` (`a limit in days` 90) `after` `the day on which the person is notified in writing of the decision or determination`)
    OR  (CONSIDER `the last day of the longer period the Minister allows`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
         WHEN JUST lastDay THEN `the day on which the person makes the request` AT MOST lastDay)

-- src:839 | 27.1 (1) A person who is dissatisfied with a decision or determination made under this Act that no benefit may be paid to the person, or respecting the amount of a benefit that may be paid to the person, may, within ninety days after the day on which the person is notified in writing of the decision or determination, or within any longer period that the Minister may, either before or after the expiration of those ninety days, allow, make a request to the Minister in the prescribed form and manner for a reconsideration of that decision or determination.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 27.1(1) (src:839)
GIVEN `the person is dissatisfied with a decision or determination made under this Act that no benefit may be paid to the person, or respecting the amount of a benefit that may be paid to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request is made within the time allowed` IS A BOOLEAN
      -- out of range: section 29 (piece oa3): Regulations
      `the request is made in the prescribed form and manner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 27.1(1): the person may make a request to the Minister for a reconsideration of the decision or determination` `the person is dissatisfied with a decision or determination made under this Act that no benefit may be paid to the person, or respecting the amount of a benefit that may be paid to the person` `the request is made within the time allowed` `the request is made in the prescribed form and manner` MEANS
        `the person is dissatisfied with a decision or determination made under this Act that no benefit may be paid to the person, or respecting the amount of a benefit that may be paid to the person`
    AND `the request is made within the time allowed`
    AND `the request is made in the prescribed form and manner`

-- (1.1): a penalty assessed under section 44.1; the person or, subject to the regulations, any person on their behalf.
-- src:841 | (1.1) A person against whom a penalty has been assessed under section 44.1 or, subject to the regulations, any person on their behalf, who is dissatisfied with the decision to impose a penalty or with the amount of the penalty may, within ninety days after the day on which the person is notified in writing of the decision or determination, or within any longer period that the Minister may, either before or after the expiration of those ninety days, allow, request the Minister in the prescribed form and manner to reconsider the decision or determination.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 27.1(1.1) (src:841)
GIVEN `a penalty has been assessed against the person under section 44.1` IS A BOOLEAN
      -- out of range: section 4(1) (piece oa3): Regulations, a request may be made on a person's behalf
      `the person, or a person on their behalf who is permitted by the regulations to do so, is dissatisfied with the decision to impose a penalty or with the amount of the penalty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request is made within the time allowed` IS A BOOLEAN
      -- out of range: section 29 (piece oa3): Regulations
      `the request is made in the prescribed form and manner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 27.1(1.1): the person may request the Minister to reconsider the decision to impose a penalty or the amount of the penalty` `a penalty has been assessed against the person under section 44.1` `the person, or a person on their behalf who is permitted by the regulations to do so, is dissatisfied with the decision to impose a penalty or with the amount of the penalty` `the request is made within the time allowed` `the request is made in the prescribed form and manner` MEANS
        `a penalty has been assessed against the person under section 44.1`
    AND `the person, or a person on their behalf who is permitted by the regulations to do so, is dissatisfied with the decision to impose a penalty or with the amount of the penalty`
    AND `the request is made within the time allowed`
    AND `the request is made in the prescribed form and manner`

-- (2): the Minister, without delay, reconsiders; may confirm or vary and may approve payment, determine the amount, or determine that no benefit is payable;
-- and, without delay, notifies the person in writing of the decision and the reasons.
-- src:843 | (2) The Minister shall, without delay after receiving a request referred to in subsection (1) or (1.1), reconsider the decision or determination, as the case may be, and may confirm or vary it and may approve payment of a benefit, determine the amount of a benefit or determine that no benefit is payable, and shall without delay notify, in writing, the person who made the request of the Minister’s decision and of the reasons for it.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 27.1(2) (src:843)
DECLARE `s 27.1(2): Outcome of a reconsideration` IS ONE OF
    `s 27.1(2): Decision confirmed`
    `s 27.1(2): Decision varied`
    `s 27.1(2): Payment of a benefit approved`
    `s 27.1(2): Amount of a benefit determined`
    `s 27.1(2): No benefit determined to be payable`

-- src:843 | (2) The Minister shall, without delay after receiving a request referred to in subsection (1) or (1.1), reconsider the decision or determination, as the case may be, and may confirm or vary it and may approve payment of a benefit, determine the amount of a benefit or determine that no benefit is payable, and shall without delay notify, in writing, the person who made the request of the Minister’s decision and of the reasons for it.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 27.1(2) (src:843)
GIVEN outcome IS A `s 27.1(2): Outcome of a reconsideration`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 27.1(2): the Minister may reach the outcome on reconsideration` outcome MEANS
    CONSIDER outcome
    WHEN `s 27.1(2): Decision confirmed` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 27.1(2): Decision varied` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 27.1(2): Payment of a benefit approved` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 27.1(2): Amount of a benefit determined` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 27.1(2): No benefit determined to be payable` THEN TRUE

-- src:843 | (2) The Minister shall, without delay after receiving a request referred to in subsection (1) or (1.1), reconsider the decision or determination, as the case may be, and may confirm or vary it and may approve payment of a benefit, determine the amount of a benefit or determine that no benefit is payable, and shall without delay notify, in writing, the person who made the request of the Minister’s decision and of the reasons for it.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 27.1(2) (src:843)
GIVEN `the Minister has received a request referred to in subsection 27.1(1) or (1.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister reconsiders the decision or determination without delay` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister notifies the person who made the request, in writing and without delay, of the Minister's decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice gives the reasons for the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 27.1(2): the Minister has done what the Minister is required to do on the request` `the Minister has received a request referred to in subsection 27.1(1) or (1.1)` `the Minister reconsiders the decision or determination without delay` `the Minister notifies the person who made the request, in writing and without delay, of the Minister's decision` `the notice gives the reasons for the decision` MEANS
        (NOT `the Minister has received a request referred to in subsection 27.1(1) or (1.1)`)
    OR  (    `the Minister reconsiders the decision or determination without delay`
         AND `the Minister notifies the person who made the request, in writing and without delay, of the Minister's decision`
         AND `the notice gives the reasons for the decision`)

§ `Appeal — benefits`

-- s 28(1): a decision of the Minister under section 27.1, including one about further time to make a request; the person or, subject to the
-- regulations, any person on their behalf.
-- src:845 | 28 (1) A person who is dissatisfied with a decision of the Minister made under section 27.1, including a decision in relation to further time to make a request, or, subject to the regulations, any person on their behalf, may appeal the decision to the Social Security Tribunal established under section 44 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 28(1) (src:845)
GIVEN `the person, or a person on their behalf who is permitted by the regulations to do so, is dissatisfied with a decision of the Minister made under section 27.1, including a decision in relation to further time to make a request` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: section 4(1) (piece oa3): Regulations, a request or appeal may be made on a person's behalf
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 28(1): the person may appeal the decision to the Social Security Tribunal` `the person, or a person on their behalf who is permitted by the regulations to do so, is dissatisfied with a decision of the Minister made under section 27.1, including a decision in relation to further time to make a request` MEANS
    `the person, or a person on their behalf who is permitted by the regulations to do so, is dissatisfied with a decision of the Minister made under section 27.1, including a decision in relation to further time to make a request`

-- (2): an income ground of appeal is referred to the Tax Court of Canada, whose decision is final and binding for all purposes of the appeal to the
-- Tribunal except in accordance with the Federal Courts Act (and subject to variation by that Court on an appeal under the Tax Court of Canada Act).
-- src:847 | (2) If, on an appeal to the Social Security Tribunal, it is a ground of the appeal that the decision made by the Minister as to the income or income from a particular source or sources of an applicant or beneficiary or of the spouse or common-law partner of the applicant or beneficiary was incorrectly made, the appeal on that ground must, in accordance with the regulations, be referred for decision to the Tax Court of Canada, whose decision, subject only to variation by that Court in accordance with any decision on an appeal under the Tax Court of Canada Act relevant to the appeal to the Social Security Tribunal, is final and binding for all purposes of the appeal to the Social Security Tribunal except in accordance with the Federal Courts Act.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 28(2) (src:847)
GIVEN `it is a ground of the appeal that the decision made by the Minister as to the income, or income from a particular source or sources, of an applicant or beneficiary or of the spouse or common-law partner of the applicant or beneficiary was incorrectly made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 28(2): the appeal on that ground must be referred for decision to the Tax Court of Canada` `it is a ground of the appeal that the decision made by the Minister as to the income, or income from a particular source or sources, of an applicant or beneficiary or of the spouse or common-law partner of the applicant or beneficiary was incorrectly made` MEANS
    `it is a ground of the appeal that the decision made by the Minister as to the income, or income from a particular source or sources, of an applicant or beneficiary or of the spouse or common-law partner of the applicant or beneficiary was incorrectly made`

-- src:847 | (2) If, on an appeal to the Social Security Tribunal, it is a ground of the appeal that the decision made by the Minister as to the income or income from a particular source or sources of an applicant or beneficiary or of the spouse or common-law partner of the applicant or beneficiary was incorrectly made, the appeal on that ground must, in accordance with the regulations, be referred for decision to the Tax Court of Canada, whose decision, subject only to variation by that Court in accordance with any decision on an appeal under the Tax Court of Canada Act relevant to the appeal to the Social Security Tribunal, is final and binding for all purposes of the appeal to the Social Security Tribunal except in accordance with the Federal Courts Act.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 28(2) (src:847)
GIVEN `the appeal on that ground has been referred to the Tax Court of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Federal Courts Act allows the decision to be departed from` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 28(2): the decision of the Tax Court of Canada is final and binding for all purposes of the appeal to the Social Security Tribunal` `the appeal on that ground has been referred to the Tax Court of Canada` `the Federal Courts Act allows the decision to be departed from` MEANS
        `the appeal on that ground has been referred to the Tax Court of Canada`
    AND (NOT `the Federal Courts Act allows the decision to be departed from`)

-- (3): the Minister may stay payment until the later of (a) the end of the period allowed for an application for judicial review and (b) where
-- Her Majesty has applied for judicial review, the month in which all proceedings in relation to it have been completed. (a) is a day and (b) a
-- month: the encoding compares (a) with the last day of the month in (b) (fork OA1-F11 of NOTES.md).
-- src:849 | (3) If a decision is made by the Social Security Tribunal in respect of a benefit, the Minister may stay payment of the benefit until the later of
-- src:850 | (a) the expiration of the period allowed for making an application under the Federal Courts Act for judicial review of the decision, and
-- src:851 | (b) where Her Majesty has made an application under the Federal Courts Act for judicial review of the decision, the month in which all proceedings in relation to the judicial review have been completed.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 28(3) (src:849-851)
GIVEN `a decision is made by the Social Security Tribunal in respect of a benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the expiration of the period allowed for making an application under the Federal Courts Act for judicial review of the decision` IS A DATE
      `the month in which all proceedings in relation to a judicial review applied for by Her Majesty have been completed` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 28(3): the last day until which the Minister may stay payment of the benefit` `a decision is made by the Social Security Tribunal in respect of a benefit` `the expiration of the period allowed for making an application under the Federal Courts Act for judicial review of the decision` `the month in which all proceedings in relation to a judicial review applied for by Her Majesty have been completed` MEANS
    IF `a decision is made by the Social Security Tribunal in respect of a benefit`
    THEN JUST (CONSIDER `the month in which all proceedings in relation to a judicial review applied for by Her Majesty have been completed`
               WHEN NOTHING THEN `the expiration of the period allowed for making an application under the Federal Courts Act for judicial review of the decision`
               WHEN JUST completed THEN `oa1: the later of two dates` `the expiration of the period allowed for making an application under the Federal Courts Act for judicial review of the decision` (`the last day of the month containing` completed))
    ELSE NOTHING
